KZ3 patch 1165: KZ3_PPU_CTX_RESTRICT=1 (lift time) qualifies each lifted function's ctx parameter __restrict. Default OFF.

Off (unset or any value but 1): the lifter emits no qualifier and no header text, so the lift is byte-identical to a lift
without this patch (tools/spu/test_vekta_ctx_restrict.sh lifts a few functions both ways and diffs them). On: the header
defines PPU_CTX_RESTRICT as __restrict (a build may define it empty to undo it without a relift) and each lifted function
is emitted as void func_X(ppu_context* PPU_CTX_RESTRICT ctx). Not applied to setjmp/longjmp functions (patch 1116: control
re-enters them through the host jump). Why it is valid: contexts live on host thread stacks, never in guest memory, and a
lifted function hands its callees ctx itself; the lifted code reaches guest memory through a byte pointer under
-fno-strict-aliasing, so without it every guest store forces ctx->fpr, ctx->vr, ctx->lr to be reloaded.
Expected gain (vekta's number, KZ1 HD, 6 alternated pairs): +1.5 % fps; ASSUMPTION for KZ3 (ppu-main is ~33.5 ms/flip), needs
a GPU A/B (see the report). Risk: any HLE or host code that writes a ctx field through a pointer other than the one it was
handed while a lifted function using that ctx is running would be undefined behaviour.
